{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-25210",
    "CVE-2026-24515",
    "CVE-2025-59375"
  ],
  "description": "It was discovered that Expat incorrectly handled memory when parsing certain\nXML files. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of\nservice. This issue was only addressed in Ubuntu 25.10. (CVE-2025-59375)\n\nIt was discovered that Expat incorrectly handled the initialization of parsers\nfor external entities. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a\ndenial of service. (CVE-2026-24515)\n\nIt was discovered that Expat incorrectly handled integer calculations when\nallocating memory for XML tags. An attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-25210)",
  "id": "USN-8022-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in Expat.",
